{
  "answer":"Your business risk assessment for NFTF activities should assess the risks associated with carrying on NFTF business, with particular focus on risks arising from the use of eKYC Systems, recognizing that distinct risks can arise in fully NFTF relationships versus mixed face-to-face/NFTF relationships. [PID:31f0a7bd-a9fa-4aab-a4b4-32d0a6fb51b2] The assessment should also identify actions to mitigate NFTF and eKYC-specific risks and refer to mitigation measures recommended by the Regulator, competent U.A.E. authorities, FATF and other relevant bodies. [PID:c24c6dfe-b5fa-4802-81ab-5894795d4362]\n\nMitigations supported in the passages include adopting appropriate measures to ensure eKYC is secure and effective, uses an appropriate combination of authentication factors, is at least as stringent as face-to-face CDD, and includes verification of the authenticity of government ID and the actual customer, applying applicable biometric technical standards guidance. [PID:aecde7ad-d719-4416-b520-a9e53a58934f] You should also pay specific attention to financial crime risks from NFTF/eKYC technology (e.g., post-onboarding transaction fraud, ML, theft of digitally stored CDD). [PID:06936741-ee7c-4307-b4eb-c86c1a6f83af]",
